# Word Limit Root Cause Consolidation

Consolidation of work from `conversation_2026-02-20_log.md`. The log documents fixes across the test creation pipeline for IELTS word limits, but a **critical gap** remains in the Firebase persistence layer that silently drops `wordLimit` before it reaches students.

## Root Cause Analysis

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["AI Parsing<br/>type-classifier"] --> B["Validation<br/>validator.service"]
    B --> C["Mapping<br/>useTestCreation"]
    C --> D["Review/Draft<br/>TestReviewPage"]
    D --> E["Firebase Storage<br/>testStorage ⚠️"]
    E --> F["Student Load<br/>useTestData"]
    F --> G["Student UI<br/>AuthenticAnswerInput<br/>IELTSQuestionsPanel"]

    style E fill:#ff4444,color:#fff
```

| Layer | Status | Detail |
|-------|--------|--------|
| AI Parsing (`type-classifier`) | ✅ Working | Extracts `wordLimit { max, min? }` correctly |
| Validation (`validator.service`) | ✅ Working | Preserves `wordLimit` on `MergedQuestion` (verified by test) |
| Mapping (`useTestCreation`) | ✅ Working | Maps `q.wordLimit?.max` to `ParsedQuestion.wordLimit` (line 329) |
| Review Page (`TestReviewPage`) | ✅ Working | Loads `wordLimit` from drafts (line 378), handles section instruction changes (lines 446-448), persists to storage format (line 600) |
| **Firebase Storage (`testStorage`)** | ❌ **THE GAP** | `saveTestToFirebase` creates a new `formatted` object (line 213) that **omits `wordLimit`**. `TestData.questions` type also **lacks `wordLimit`**. |
| Student Load (`useTestData`) | ⚠️ Passive | Passes raw `TestData` through — if Firebase has it, students get it |
| Student UI components | ✅ Working | `getMaxWordsForType` accepts `manualLimit` override; `getTaskInstructions` accepts `wordLimit` param; `groupQuestionsByTaskType` passes `firstQ.wordLimit` |

> [!CAUTION]
> Despite all upstream fixes being correctly implemented, the Firebase persistence layer (`testStorage.ts` lines 212-234) silently drops `wordLimit` when creating the `formatted` question object. **Every test published through this function has `wordLimit: undefined` in Firebase**, causing all student views to fall back to hardcoded defaults.

## Proposed Changes

### Firebase Storage Layer

#### [MODIFY] [testStorage.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sanctuary/Desktop/Homework%20App/kahoot/src/services/testStorage.ts)

**1. Add `wordLimit` to `TestData.questions` type** (line ~127-139):

```diff
 questions: Array<{
     number: number;
     type: string;
     question: string;
     options?: string[];
     answer: string | string[] | Record<string, string>;
     passageId: string;
     resourceId?: string;
     sectionNumber?: number;
     points: number;
     explanation?: string;
     acceptableAnswers?: string[];
+    wordLimit?: number;
+    sectionInstructionId?: string;
 }>;
```

**2. Persist `wordLimit` in `saveTestToFirebase` question formatting** (line ~212-234):

```diff
 const formatted: any = {
     number: question.number || index + 1,
     type: question.type,
     question: question.question,
     answer: question.answer,
     passageId: question.passageId || (passages[0]?.id || 'default'),
     points: question.points || 1,
 };

 if (question.options && question.options.length > 0) {
     formatted.options = question.options;
 }
+if (question.wordLimit !== undefined && question.wordLimit > 0) {
+    formatted.wordLimit = question.wordLimit;
+}
+if (question.sectionInstructionId) {
+    formatted.sectionInstructionId = question.sectionInstructionId;
+}
```

**3. Add diagnostic logging** after question formatting:

```diff
+// Diagnostic: Log wordLimit statistics for debugging
+const questionsWithWordLimit = formattedQuestions.filter((q: any) => q.wordLimit);
+if (questionsWithWordLimit.length > 0) {
+    console.log(`📏 [TestStorage] ${questionsWithWordLimit.length}/${formattedQuestions.length} questions have wordLimit set`);
+}
```

